# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# ESP32-P4 with external PSRAM.
#
# With the APTA 1.0 API, the Phase 7 global-beatgrid configuration needs 603,504 bytes
# of workspace. It completes on the P4 v1.3 with internal memory only, averaging
# 12,738 us per process call for that feature set.
#
# With these settings the same board reports 32 MB of PSRAM and every feature
# set runs. Phase 7 measured the cooperative global-grid profile at 2,670 us
# average, p99 <= 6,000 us and 10,295 us maximum. See the Phase 7 bounded-refresh
# status document; sections 29 and 30 of the S4 status document retain the
# pre-Phase-7 workspace/placement history.
#
# Use alongside sdkconfig.defaults:
#
#   idf.py -B build-esp32p4 \
#     -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.p4.defaults" \
#     set-target esp32p4 build
#
# ESP-IDF 6.0.2 builds P4 firmware requiring chip revision v3.1 or newer. A
# v1.x board needs 5.5, which supports v0.0 through v1.0.
CONFIG_SPIRAM=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_HEX=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_SPEED_20M=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_MALLOC=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_TRY_ALLOCATE_WIFI_LWIP=y
CONFIG_APTA_OVERVIEW_FRAMES_PER_COLUMN=32768
CONFIG_APTA_MAX_DETAIL_TILES=4
CONFIG_APTA_ONSET_BIN_CAPACITY=4096
CONFIG_APTA_GLOBAL_BIN_CAPACITY=16384
